<title>UK: John Lewis UK weekly store sales up 8.5 percent.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK weekly store sales up 8.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 8.5 percent in the week to November 9 compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the 15 weeks to November 9, sales were up 15.0 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 8.4 percent in the week and were up 12.1 percent in the 15-week period.</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
